===H===
* [[Hapanvelli]]{{spaced ndash}} a traditional Southeastern [[Finnish cuisine|Finnish]] dish that resembles [[pea soup]] but has a more sour flavor.
* [[Harees]]{{spaced ndash}} a [[Middle Eastern cuisine|Middle Eastern dish]] of boiled, cracked, or coarsely-ground [[wheat]] and [[meat]] or [[Chicken (food)|chicken]]. Its consistency varies between a porridge and a [[dumpling]].
* [[Hasty pudding]]{{spaced ndash}} a [[pudding]] or porridge of [[cereal|grains]] cooked in milk or water.  In the [[United States]], it invariably refers to a version made of ground maize. Hasty pudding is notably mentioned in a verse of the early American song ''[[Yankee Doodle]]''.
* [[Helmipuuro]]{{spaced ndash}} traditional in [[Finland]] and in [[Russia]], this porridge is made from [[monodisperse]] grains of [[potato starch]] that are swelled in boiling milk into translucent "pearls" of about 5&nbsp;mm in diameter, thus the name ''helmipuuro'' ("pearl porridge").
* [[Hobakjuk]]{{spaced ndash}} a variety of ''[[Juk (food)|juk]]'', or [[Korean cuisine|Korean]] porridge, made with steamed [[pumpkin]] or [[Squash (plant)|squash]] and [[glutinous rice]] flour or rice soaked in water.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://100.empas.com/dicsearch/pentry.html?s=K&i=276464&v=47 |title=Hobakjuk (호박죽 ―粥)|publisher=[[Empas]] / [[EncyKorea]] |access-date=2008-08-17|language=ko}}</ref>
